<instruction name="VSCALEFSD">
 <copyright>Copyright (C) Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.</copyright>
 <shortdesc>Scale Scalar Float64 Values With Float64 Values</shortdesc>
 <longdesc><para unique="1046139">
   <string>Performs a floating-point scale of the scalar double precision floating-point value in the first source operand by multiplying it by 2 to the power of the double precision floating-point value in second source operand.</string></para>
  <para unique="1046140">
   <string>The equation of this operation is given by:</string></para>
  <para unique="1046141">
   <string>xmm1 := xmm2*2</string><superscript><string>floor(xmm3)</string></superscript><string>.</string></para>
  <para unique="1046142">
   <string>Floor(xmm3) means maximum integer value &#8804; xmm3.</string></para>
  <para unique="1046143">
   <string>If the result cannot be represented in double precision, then the proper overflow response (for positive scaling operand), or the proper underflow response (for negative scaling operand) is issued. The overflow and underflow responses are dependent on the rounding mode (for IEEE-compliant rounding), as well as on other settings in MXCSR (exception mask bits, FTZ bit), and on the SAE bit.</string></para>
  <para unique="1046144">
   <string>EVEX encoded version: The first source operand is an XMM register. The second source operand is an XMM register or a memory location. The destination operand is an XMM register conditionally updated with writemask k1.</string></para>
  <para unique="1046147">
   <string>Handling of special-case input values are listed in </string><link linkend="43524: 06_Table: Table 5-30. \VSCALEFPD Special Cases"><string>Table 5&#8209;37</string></link><string> and </string><link linkend="36948: 06_Table: Table 5-31. Additional VSCALEFPD/SD Special Cases"><string>Table 5&#8209;38</string></link><string>.</string></para>
  </longdesc>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting><string>VSCALEFSD __m128d _mm_scalef_round_sd(__m128d a, __m128d b, int);</string><string>
</string><string>VSCALEFSD __m128d _mm_mask_scalef_round_sd(__m128d s, __mmask8 k, __m128d a, __m128d b, int);</string><string>
</string><string>VSCALEFSD __m128d _mm_maskz_scalef_round_sd(__mmask8 k, __m128d a, __m128d b, int);</string><string>
</string></programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1046187">
   <string>Overflow, Underflow, Invalid, Precision, Denormal (for Src1).</string></para>
  <para unique="1046188">
   <string>Denormal is not reported for Src2.</string></para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1046193">
   <string>See </string><link linkend="63155: 06_Table: Table 2-47. Type E3 Class Exception Conditions"><string>Table&#160;2&#8209;49, &#8220;Type E3 Class Exception Conditions.&#8221;</string></link></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
